import{h as e,m as t,u as a,i as o,n as r,q as n,v as s,x as i,f as l,k as d,e as c,j as u,d as h,s as p,c as m,a as y,g,p as k}from"./raid-BDqEtYFD.js";import{a as f}from"./cinematics-DdxhWjU-.js";const b={"guide.next":"Next","guide.prev":"Back","guide.skip":"Skip","guide.never":"Don’t show again","guide.done":"Let’s go!","guide.rewards":"Rewards","guide.help":"Mode guide","guide.page":"{n} / {total}","guide.story.title":"Story","guide.story.1.t":"Your Story run","guide.story.1.b":`Pick a champion and a difficulty (Ascension 0 to 10), then cross 4 acts up to the final boss.
Acts 1 to 3 follow your realm’s campaign; act 4 is shared by everyone.
On the map, choose your road: fights, elites (skull), campfires, merchants, “?” events and treasures.`,"guide.story.2.t":"Rules of the road","guide.story.2.b":`Every fight is a duel. After each win, add one card to your deck (or skip).
Your HP does not come back on its own: heal at campfires. Beating an act boss heals you fully.
The Crowns you earn on the way are spent at merchants (cards, relics, potions). They only last for this Story run.`,"guide.story.3.t":"Getting started","guide.story.3.b":`A few good cards beat many average ones: don’t be afraid to skip.
Elites are tough, but they always drop a relic and a piece of gear.`,"guide.story.rw":`Each act boss beaten: 1 booster. Class and Season Pass XP for every fight.
The full list of Gold and Shard rewards is in the Shop guide.`,"guide.abyss.title":"The Abyss","guide.abyss.1.t":"An endless descent","guide.abyss.1.b":`Beneath the World Tower lies the Abyss of the Breach: each depth is a new, harder act.
You keep your deck and relics; your HP is restored. No more boss relics down there.
At each depth, enemies gain 30% HP and 3 armor.`,"guide.abyss.2.t":"The corruption","guide.abyss.2.b":`From turn 8 of a fight, the corruption of the Abyss burns you: end your fights quickly.
Save your heals and potions for the depth bosses.
Falling ruins nothing: your Story run stays a victory, and every depth counts.`,"guide.abyss.rw":`Each depth cleared: +45 Gold and +15 Shards, on top of the victory (90 Gold + 40 Shards).
Each depth boss: 1 Breach booster.`,"guide.duel.title":"Duel","guide.duel.1.t":"The basics","guide.duel.1.b":`Two champions with 30 HP, each with a 30-card deck. Bring the enemy HP down to 0.
Mana: 1 crystal on the first turn, then one more each turn (10 at most). It refills every turn.
Mulligan: at the start, swap out the expensive cards in your hand. The second player gets “The Coin” (1 extra mana, once).`,"guide.duel.2.t":"How to play","guide.duel.2.b":`Drag a card onto the board to play it, then drag a minion onto a target to attack.
A new minion sleeps for a turn (unless it has Charge or Rush). An enemy with Taunt must be hit first.
A turn lasts 75 seconds; the rope burns for the last 20. Finish with “End turn”.`,"guide.duel.3.t":"Choose your opponent","guide.duel.3.b":`Practice (AI): perfect to test a deck, at the level you like.
Online: create a game and share its code, or join a friend’s. The “Ranked” tile finds an opponent of your rank.
Same screen: two players on one device, no rewards.`,"guide.duel.rw":`Online win: 40 Gold + 8 Shards (vs the AI: 23 Gold + 3 Shards). Loss: 14 Gold (vs the AI: 6 Gold). First win of the day: +55 Gold and +15 Shards.
No limit on paid games per day (Champion: +6 Gold per win). Online, friendly and ranked: 5 paid games per day against the same opponent.
A game shorter than 4 turns pays nothing.`,"guide.ranked.title":"Ranked","guide.ranked.1.t":"The ranked season","guide.ranked.1.b":`In the Duel lobby, turn on “Ranked match” and play online. You need an account with a confirmed email.
The server checks every game and draws the host at random. If it is unreachable or being updated, the game is “unverified”: it gives no season reward. If the wait runs long, you may face an opponent trained by the game; like any player, it also serves its realm in the War of the Three Realms.
6 tiers of 3 divisions: Combatant, Challenger, Rival, Duelist, Elite, Gladiator. You start at Combatant II.`,"guide.ranked.2.t":"Climbing well","guide.ranked.2.b":`Elo rating: against an opponent of the same rating, the winner takes what the loser loses. Your first 10 games (placement) count about double (±20), then ±12.
Chain wins: from the 3rd in a row, +50% (8 points at most). Conceding = a normal loss; a cancelled game costs nothing (2 a day, beyond that = a loss).
Against the same opponent, at most 60 points change hands per day. A season lasts a month; at the next one, your rating moves halfway back to the start. Heroic Ranked: same rules, its own rating; if the wait runs long, you may face an opponent trained by the game there too (cards at the level of its Renown). Between games these opponents also play each other: their games, rating and history are simulated by the server.`,"guide.ranked.rw":`Every game pays like an online duel (no daily limit; 5 paid games per day against the same opponent).
First time you reach each division in a season: Gold, Shards, and a booster in division I.
End of season, by your best tier: from 115 Gold + 1 booster (Combatant) to 1150 Gold + 4 boosters + frame, card back and title (Gladiator).`,"guide.team.title":"Team duel (2v2)","guide.team.1.t":"Two against two","guide.team.1.b":`You and your teammate each keep your own hero (30 HP), deck and mana.
The team board is shared: 8 minions at most.
You play at the same time: the turn passes when you are both done. No chat: work together with the 4 team signals.`,"guide.team.2.t":"Special rules","guide.team.2.b":`A Taunt minion protects both heroes of the team. If a hero falls, their minions go to their teammate; the team loses when both are dead.
Your “your minions” effects and Spell Damage only apply to you, not your ally.
An area spell hits a single opponent: the one you target, otherwise the one with the most minions.`,"guide.team.3.t":"Finding a team","guide.team.3.b":`Vs the AI: one ally and two opponents played by the AI.
With a friend: share the room’s 6-letter code.
Group search: if nobody shows up, the AI fills the team after 45 seconds.`,"guide.team.rw":`Like a duel: “AI” rates if an AI plays, “online” rates if all four players are human.
First win of the day: +55 Gold and +15 Shards. 2v2 is never ranked.`,"guide.brawl.title":"Brawl","guide.brawl.1.t":"One wild rule a week","guide.brawl.1.b":`Each week, a special rule changes the duel: random decks, everything costs 1, double draw, 60 HP heroes…
The rule and the deck you will play are shown on this screen.
Play against the AI, or open a room to challenge a friend.`,"guide.brawl.2.t":"Getting started","guide.brawl.2.b":`Read the rule carefully: it often changes the best strategy.
In random-deck weeks every card is lent to you: a chance to try the ones you don’t own.
Second tab: the “Rule of the week”, a small twist on the classic duel (20 HP heroes, +1/+1 minions…) that also changes every Wednesday.`,"guide.brawl.rw":`First win of the week: 1 free booster, in the Brawl and in the Rule of the week alike.
Each game also pays like a duel (vs the AI or friendly online).`,"guide.heroic.title":"Heroic challenges","guide.heroic.1.t":"The bosses return","guide.heroic.1.b":`Face the 9 Story bosses in heroic form: more HP, armor, a second phase and a legendary of their own.
Act 1 bosses are open right away; beating a boss of an act opens those of the next act.
You play your duel deck.`,"guide.heroic.2.t":"Getting started","guide.heroic.2.b":`Read the boss’s hero power and phase 2 before you pick your champion.
Bring answers to big minions: bosses play Ascension 10 decks.
You can retry as often as you like.`,"guide.heroic.rw":`First win against each boss: heroic card back and portrait frame (and your champion’s heroic look, if it has one).
All 9 bosses beaten: a title.
No Gold, but games count for daily quests.`,"guide.friends.title":"Friends","guide.friends.1.t":"Beat my deck!","guide.friends.1.b":`“Create a challenge” gives a link that shares your duel deck.
Your friend plays it against the same AI, then sends back a result link: paste it with “Paste a link”.
Ranking: any win beats any loss; then fewer turns and more HP left come first.`,"guide.friends.2.t":"Getting started","guide.friends.2.b":`Send the link through any messaging app.
Take on your friends’ challenges too, to compare your decks.`,"guide.friends.rw":"No Gold: just honor… and daily quests (duels played, cards played, minions summoned).","guide.rvr.title":"War of the Three Realms","guide.rvr.1.t":"Defend your realm","guide.rvr.1.b":`Your allegiance (Logres, Nordmark or Eriu) decides your Story campaign and the frontier you defend.
Every win earns Renown for your realm and raises your renown rank.
A class from another realm earns only half the Renown.`,"guide.rvr.2.t":"Sieges","guide.rvr.2.b":`A tower can always be attacked. A keep needs the tower of its region; a relic keep needs the whole frontier.
A siege is 2 or 3 fights in a row: you keep your HP, with a short respite between them.
The gate has Taunt: break it down. Ram, Trebuchet and War Horn join your deck.`,"guide.rvr.3.t":"Getting started","guide.rvr.3.b":`Start with towers: they open the keeps.
Defend threatened sites: left alone, they fall 2 days later.
Each renown rank gives you +3 HP in sieges.`,"guide.rvr.rw":`Tower: 35 Gold · keep: 65 Gold · relic: 105 Gold (plus Shards and Renown). Total victory: +140 Gold and +50 Shards.
Every week: rewards by your realm’s rank and your personal tiers (up to 2 boosters and a title).
Changing allegiance costs 300 Gold (at most once every 7 days).`,"guide.shop.title":"Shop","guide.shop.1.t":"Spend your Gold","guide.shop.1.b":`Gold is earned in every mode and spent here. Seven tabs: Boosters, Classes, Daily deals, Armory, Decks, Premium shop and Season Pass.
Realm booster: 100 Gold · class booster: 120 Gold. A bundle of 10 costs the price of 9.
Armory: 6 pieces of gear a day, each sold only once.`,"guide.shop.2.t":"Getting started","guide.shop.2.b":`Class boosters only hold one champion’s cards: ideal to complete a specific deck.
Your boosters wait in the Boosters tab: open them whenever you like.
Everything can be earned by playing: the Premium shop is optional.`,"guide.shop.rw":`Story: 23 Gold + 5 Shards, then 45 Gold + 15 Shards per act, 7 Gold + 2 Shards per fight, 90 Gold + 40 Shards if you win. First Story run of the day: +70 Gold and +25 Shards.
All daily quests: 2 realm boosters + 170 Gold. Quests also fill the weekly realm chest, opened every Wednesday at 3:00 UTC (4:00 in Paris in winter).
Free login calendar: 7 days of gifts (Gold, Shards, boosters).`,"guide.boosters.title":"Boosters","guide.boosters.1.t":"Opening a booster","guide.boosters.1.b":`5 cards per booster, at least 1 of them rare or better.
Tear the booster open, then flip the cards one by one.
A card can come out golden: same effect, more shine, and it is worth 4 times more Shards.`,"guide.boosters.2.t":"Guarantees","guide.boosters.2.b":`At least one epic every 10 boosters and one legendary every 40.
Very rare: 1 booster in 1,000 is a god pack, 5 epics or legendaries!
Spare duplicates can be disenchanted into Shards in the Collection.`,"guide.boosters.rw":`Cards join your Collection and your duel decks.
Odds per card: legendary 0.75%, epic 3.5%, rare 20%.`,"guide.collection.title":"Collection","guide.collection.1.t":"Your cards","guide.collection.1.b":`All your cards, with search and filters (realm, class, cost, rarity).
Starter, common and uncommon cards are always playable; rares and better must be owned.
Select a card to read, craft or disenchant it.`,"guide.collection.2.t":"Crafting","guide.collection.2.b":`Crafting costs Shards: rare 100, epic 400, legendary 1600 (a golden one costs 4 times more).
Disenchanting gives Shards back: rare 20, epic 100, legendary 400.
“Disenchant duplicates” keeps 2 copies of each card (1 of a legendary): no risk.`,"guide.collection.rw":"Shards are earned in Story, in duels, from daily quests and achievements.","guide.upgrades.title":"Upgrades","guide.upgrades.1.t":"Permanent bonuses","guide.upgrades.1.b":`Invest your Gold in bonuses that apply to all your Story runs.
+1 max HP for a champion (60 Gold, up to 5 times) · +1 potion slot (120 Gold, up to 5).
+1 starting Crown in every Story run (50 Gold) · new champion: 400 Gold.`,"guide.upgrades.2.t":"Getting started","guide.upgrades.2.b":`One more potion slot often saves a boss fight.
Max HP is bought per champion: invest in your favorite first.`,"guide.upgrades.rw":"Nothing to earn here: everything is paid with the Gold earned in the game modes.","guide.codex.title":"Codex","guide.codex.1.t":"The book of discoveries","guide.codex.1.b":`The Codex keeps everything you have met: cards, relics and enemies.
An entry is revealed the first time you meet it or obtain it.
Select an entry to read its effect and its story.`,"guide.codex.2.t":"Getting started","guide.codex.2.b":`Read up on enemies before a boss to learn their powers.
Filter cards by expansion, such as the Breach.
“Lessons” tab: short guided duels to learn Combo, Overload, Secret… (a small reward the first time).`,"guide.codex.rw":"Achievements: “Scholar of Camelot” (60 cards discovered) and “Bestiary” (15 enemies).","guide.decks.title":"My decks","guide.decks.1.t":"Building a deck","guide.decks.1.b":`A duel deck holds exactly 30 cards: your class’s cards and neutrals.
2 copies at most per card, only 1 of a legendary.
Rares, epics and legendaries must be in your Collection.`,"guide.decks.2.t":"Tools and tips","guide.decks.2.b":`“Auto fill” completes your deck in one go. Copy a deck code to share it, or paste a friend’s.
Aim mostly for 1-3 mana cards to start well, and a few big cards to finish.
Then pick this deck in the Duel lobby.`,"guide.decks.rw":"No direct reward: a good deck pays off in Duel, Ranked and Heroic challenges.","guide.gear.title":"Equipment","guide.gear.1.t":"Equip your champions","guide.gear.1.b":`13 slots per champion: HP, armor, Strength, healing, an extra starting card, mana on the first turn…
A full set gives extra bonuses.
The bag (80 items) is shared by all your champions.`,"guide.gear.2.t":"Where gear comes from","guide.gear.2.b":`Story loot (always from elites, bosses and treasures), the Shop’s Armory, merchants, sieges.
Gear is locked in at the start of a Story run, and it loses power above Ascension 5.
Full bag: new items are disenchanted into Shards.`,"guide.gear.rw":"Sell or disenchant useless items to get Gold or Shards back.","guide.quests.title":"Quests","guide.quests.1.t":"New quests every day","guide.quests.1.b":`5 quests every day at midnight UTC (6 with the Realm Pass), shown on the main menu.
They progress by themselves as you play: a Story act (any champion), duels (the Arena too, in the Duel lobby), cards played…
Every day, one of the 5 quests shows the booster icon: finish it for 1 booster of your realm on top.`,"guide.quests.2.t":"Milestones and catch-up","guide.quests.2.b":`3 daily quests done: 1 booster of your realm. All 5: 2 realm boosters + 170 Gold on top.
An unfinished quest stays 1 more day, tagged “yesterday” (3 at most). It does not count for the milestones.
Every quest also fills the weekly realm chest, opened every Wednesday at 3:00 UTC (4:00 in Paris in winter).`,"guide.quests.3.t":"Weekly quests","guide.quests.3.b":`“Weekly” tab: 3 longer quests (10 duel wins, 2 Story runs, 5 boosters opened…).
New quests every Wednesday at 3:00 UTC (4:00 in Paris in winter, 5:00 in summer), with the realm chest, the Arena ticket and the brawl.`,"guide.quests.rw":`Daily quest: 40 to 115 Gold + 5 to 20 Shards. Weekly quest: 170 to 290 Gold + 30 to 40 Shards (+1 booster for the longest).
Each quest: +40 class XP, +100 Season Pass XP and Renown.`,"guide.seasonPass.title":"Season Pass","guide.seasonPass.1.t":"The Season Pass","guide.seasonPass.1.b":`30 tiers of 400 XP over the season (one month). Everything you play gives XP.
Free track: Gold, Shards, a booster every 5 tiers and a card back at tier 30.
A forgotten tier is paid automatically at the end of the season. Behind? Your XP counts double.`,"guide.seasonPass.2.t":"Class levels","guide.seasonPass.2.b":`Each class levels up from 1 to 50 with the XP of its games (“Class levels” screen).
Every level gives a reward: a booster of its realm every 5 levels, a cosmetic every 10.`,"guide.seasonPass.rw":`XP: fight 20, elite 35, boss 60, duel win 60, daily quest 100 (Pass).
Realm Pass (optional): a premium track with more rewards.`,"guide.classLevels.title":"Class levels","guide.classLevels.1.t":"Level up your classes","guide.classLevels.1.b":`Each class levels up from 1 to 50 with the XP of its games: Story, duels, the Arena, quests.
Every level gives a reward: Gold, Shards, class cards, a booster of its realm every 5 levels, a cosmetic every 10.
Tap (or hover) a level of the track to see its reward.`,"guide.classLevels.2.t":"Heroic Mode and mastery","guide.classLevels.2.b":`At level 10, a class opens Heroic Mode.
At level 50, it earns the master crown.
A locked class already earns its levels in the Arena and Brawls, which lend it.`,"guide.classLevels.rw":`Class XP: fight 20, elite 35, boss 60, duel win 60, quest 40.
Every level reward is paid at once.`,"guide.achievements.title":"Achievements","guide.achievements.1.t":"Feats to accomplish","guide.achievements.1.b":`Beat bosses, win sieges, complete your collection… across every mode.
They unlock by themselves: a banner shows up when you earn one.
Some give a title or a portrait frame.`,"guide.achievements.2.t":"Getting started","guide.achievements.2.b":`Tap an achievement to see everything: how to get it, your progress and its rewards, with a preview of the title or frame.
Collection achievements say which cards count and open your collection on the missing ones.`,"guide.achievements.rw":"Most pay Gold and Shards according to their difficulty; the big goals give a title or a frame.","guide.leaderboard.title":"Leaderboard","guide.leaderboard.1.t":"Measure yourself","guide.leaderboard.1.b":`Your boards: Ranked (season), Story records, Crowns earned and Friends (your friends’ rating, wins this week, best expedition). Then Guilds (every guild of the three realms) and Realms (this week’s War and the players earning the most Renown).
Story score: 1000 per act, +5000 for a win, +500 per boss, then +25% per Ascension level.
Online, you compare yourself with every player; offline, with your own Story runs.`,"guide.leaderboard.2.t":"Getting started","guide.leaderboard.2.b":`Raise the Ascension to multiply your Story score.
The Ranked board follows your rating for the current season.
The ranked opponents trained by the game also appear on the Story and Daily Challenge boards (runs simulated by the server, always below the best player).`,"guide.leaderboard.rw":"No direct reward: glory! Ranked pays at the end of the season."},w={"modes.section":"Special modes","modes.brawl":"Brawl","modes.heroic":"Heroic challenges","modes.friends":"Friends","brawl.title":"Brawl of the week","brawl.week":"Week {week} · next brawl in {time}","brawl.rulesLabel":"Brawl rules","brawl.reward":"First win of the week: 1 free booster","brawl.rewardDone":"Weekly booster earned · {n} win(s)","brawl.vsBot":"Play vs the AI","brawl.withFriend":"Challenge a friend (room)","brawl.champion":"Champion","brawl.deckRandom":"Your deck is drawn at random from your class cards.","brawl.deckCommons":"Your deck is built from common cards only.","brawl.deckOwn":"You play your duel deck: {deck}.","brawl.boosterWon":"Brawl won: free booster!","brawl.lobbyBanner":"Brawl: {name}","brawl.errMismatch":"Your friend is not playing the same brawl (different week?).","brawl.randomDecks.name":"Random decks","brawl.randomDecks.rules":"Each hero gets a random 30-card deck of their class. Every card is on loan!","brawl.allCostOne.name":"Everything costs 1","brawl.allCostOne.rules":"Every card costs at most 1 mana. Legendaries on turn 1!","brawl.commonsOnly.name":"Commons only","brawl.commonsOnly.rules":"Decks only hold common cards, drawn at random from your class.","brawl.doublePower.name":"Two hero powers","brawl.doublePower.rules":"Your hero power can be used twice per turn.","brawl.echoMinions.name":"Echo of the dead","brawl.echoMinions.rules":"Minions have only 1 HP, but have “Deathrattle: summon a copy of this minion” (the copy stays dead).","brawl.doubleDraw.name":"Double draw","brawl.doubleDraw.rules":"Each hero draws 2 cards at the start of their turn.","brawl.fullMana.name":"Max mana from turn 1","brawl.fullMana.rules":"Each hero starts every turn with 10 mana crystals.","brawl.giants.name":"